  "$comment": "Hand-kept device facts that no machine-readable source carries. Safe-area insets are CSS px in portrait (top, bottom) and landscape (side = the notch or Dynamic Island side and its mirror, bottom = the home indicator). 'measured' is per mode: 'browser' turns true once tools/devices/measure-safe-area.mjs has read the insets in Mobile Safari in the iOS Simulator (env(safe-area-inset-*) in a viewport-fit=cover page); 'fullscreen' stays false until they are read in a full-screen web view (Safari cannot report the portrait top inset, which its bars cover). Until then they are public figures and may be off by a few px. Groups are looked up by model name (Playwright's device names); a measured model is split into a group of its own. 'screen' is the portrait screen in CSS px, for reference. A model missing here (iPhone Air) has no known safe area: its checks carry no safeArea, so the safe-area-target rule does not run on them, and a viewport-fit=cover page that reads env(safe-area-inset-*) is Unknown there.",
